<BaseLayout title="SEO API Cost Benchmark: Same-Workload Methodology (2026)" description="How Search Data Bench will compare SEO API cost on the same locked workload without inventing cross-provider equivalence.">
<section class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Cost research · Protocol boundary</p><h1>SEO API cost benchmark: same workload, observable cost</h1>
<div class="notice"><strong>Results not published yet:</strong> the comparable three-provider production workload has not been executed. This page defines the commercial question without inventing a cost winner.</div>
<h2>What will be measured</h2><p>For the locked Benchmark #1 workload we retain provider-reported or directly observable request cost, successful and limited calls, missing fields and runner latency. Subscription price alone is not treated as cost per comparable result.</p>
<h2>What we already know</h2><p>A prior SE Ranking frozen run had a direct monetary cost of $0 under the available account and an observed API-unit delta of 1,020. That run was not SDB-B01 and therefore cannot be used as an apples-to-apples cost result against DataForSEO or Mangools.</p>
<h2>Why the result is pending</h2><p>DataForSEO comparable workload cost and Mangools authenticated API entitlement/cost remain unresolved in our evidence. We preserve those gaps instead of filling them from unrelated plan prices.</p>
<p><a href="/benchmarks/search-data-benchmark-01/">Read the locked protocol →</a></p></section>
